{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-lev-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.82: `scale-county-lev` -- `userdb-lev` in SINGLE-county domain: the same selection (THC, CO, NOx, NMHC and the PM2.5 group at running and start exhaust for 21, 31 and 32, every fuel MOVES adds, Washtenaw, 2020, August, weekday, hour 7) over scale-county's COUNTY database (`washtenaw_cdb`, setup-county.sql) with the same LEV database as a second, USER input database (`washtenaw_lev`; `inputs/washtenaw-county-lev.esm`).\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is the merge order across three databases: MasterLoop merges the user database, then the county database, then the default database, each with INSERT IGNORE. The county database holds no emissionRateByAge, so the execution table is again the default's at the run's pollutant-processes with the 48,657 LEV values in place (1,384,677 rows, reproduced exactly in pandas), and because scale-county's database holds the default's own rows for 2020, the output equals `userdb-lev`'s cell for cell. It is the LEV merge read through the SINGLE-domain catalogue chain rather than the DEFAULT one.\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to the chain's `rateSurvivorCount`; `n_sourceBin` 2 and `n_physicsRow` 7 as in `userdb-lev`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "user-input-database",
      "lev"
    ]
  },
